.TH EVENT_LOOP_CONSTRUCT_SCOPED 3 "2026-07-12" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
event_loop_construct_scoped \- declare, initialise, and auto-destroy an event_loop on scope exit
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

event_loop_construct_scoped(name, max_events_per_wait, num_lock_stripes,
                            num_reactor_threads);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Declares an event_loop variable named name tagged with a GCC/Clang
cleanup attribute, calls event_loop_create() to initialise it, and calls
fatal_err() if creation fails.  The variable is automatically destroyed
(every reactor thread shut down and joined, all registrations freed)
when it goes out of scope, without an explicit event_loop_destroy()
call.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
name                  Variable name for the event_loop handle.
max_events_per_wait   Size of the epoll_wait batch buffer each reactor
                      thread uses (must be between 1 and INT_MAX
                      inclusive, and small enough that
                      max_events_per_wait * sizeof(struct epoll_event)
                      does not overflow size_t).
num_lock_stripes      Number of independent lock stripes for the fd/entry
                      registry (must be >= 1).  1 means a single
                      shared lock.
num_reactor_threads   Number of background reactor threads (must be
                      >= 1; 1 means a single thread that both polls
                      and dispatches inline).
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Calls fatal_err() on failure.  A caller relying on no callback still
being able to reference anything reachable through this loop's scope
(e.g. a mutex or buffer a callback's arg points at) must ensure that
reliance holds up to and including the scope-exit join, not just an
explicit event_loop_remove(3) call beforehand; see
event_loop_remove(3)'s own notes on a callback outliving that call's
return, which this scope's implicit shutdown is equally subject to.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
{
    event_loop_construct_scoped(loop, 32, 1, 1);
    event_reg reg = event_loop_add(loop, selectable_from_fd(fd, ccol_select_read),
                                    handlers, NULL, NULL);
    /* ... */
}  /* loop is automatically shut down (every reactor thread joined) and
      destroyed here */
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR event_loop_construct (3),
.BR event_loop_declare_scoped (3),
.BR event_loop_create (3),
.BR event_loop_remove (3)
